#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:1
msgid "ADR-0016: MCP server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P13.2 (REQ-MCP-1, REQ-MCP-2); completed by P13.3 to P13.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:9
msgid ""
"AI assistants (Claude Code, Claude Desktop, other MCP clients) must "
"build, run and analyse simulations through the Model Context Protocol, "
"with the same results as the Python API (objective O4) and the safeguards"
" of the service layer (ADR-0015). The official Python SDK changed its "
"server API in version 2: `FastMCP` became `MCPServer`, and the protocol "
"revision 2026-07-28 replaced the requests sent by the server in the "
"middle of a call (elicitation, sampling) by results asking the client for"
" input (`InputRequiredResult`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:15
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:17
msgid ""
"`lumos.mcp.create_server(service)` builds an `MCPServer` of the SDK 2 "
"(`mcp>=2.3,<3`, extra `mcp`). `lumos mcp` serves it over stdio; the logs "
"go to stderr, since stdout carries the protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:19
msgid ""
"Each tool translates its arguments into one call of "
"`lumos.service.Service` and returns the Pydantic model of the service "
"(structured content and JSON text). The tools have the names of REQ-"
"MCP-2; their docstrings are their descriptions, written for a language "
"model (units as text, ports as `\"element.port\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:22
msgid ""
"A server holds one session of the service, of origin `mcp`, so its runs "
"and actions are journaled as such."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:23
msgid ""
"**Current context**: the last context created, loaded, imported or named "
"by a tool. Tools take an optional `context` and use the current one when "
"it is omitted, which keeps the conversations short."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:25
msgid ""
"**Errors**: a `ServiceError` becomes a `ToolError` whose text holds the "
"message, the hint and the code, so that the assistant can fix its "
"request; other exceptions are reported with their type and message rather"
" than the SDK's generic \"Error executing tool\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:28
msgid ""
"**Runs**: `run` starts a job of the service, reports its progress with "
"MCP progress notifications while it waits (up to `wait_seconds`) and "
"returns the job; longer runs continue in the background (`get_job`, "
"`wait_job`). Without `outputs`, the main outputs of the context (those of"
" its preset) are computed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:31
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Resources** (P13.3) use the scheme `lumos://`: `docs` and "
"`docs/{+path}`, `elements` and `elements/{type_id}`, `presets` and "
"`presets/{name}`, `context/current` (and its `journal`), `contexts/{id}` "
"and `contexts/{id}/journal`, `archives` and `archives/{+path}` (relative "
"to the archive directory; the SDK rejects `..` and absolute paths). "
"**Prompts** guide four use cases: `design_instrument`, "
"`estimate_detection`, `calibrate_bench`, `diagnose_simulation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:36
msgid ""
"**Responses** (P13.5): signals are answered with a short text summary "
"(kind, shape, range and mean with their unit, grid, wavelength) and a PNG"
" image, runs with one line naming the job and the next tool; the Pydantic"
" model stays the structured content (`Annotated[CallToolResult, Model]`),"
" without the figure bytes. The values shown are accepted back as they "
"are, and a quantity without unit is refused with an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:40
msgid ""
"**HTTP** (P13.6): `lumos mcp --transport http` serves the streamable HTTP"
" application of the SDK with uvicorn on `127.0.0.1:8765/mcp`; "
"`create_http_app` returns it for the web backend to mount. Without "
"authentication (P14), another address needs `--allow-remote`, and the "
"operation of equipment is refused for remote clients, who could confirm "
"their own actions. The SDK protects loopback servers from DNS rebinding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:45
msgid ""
"Synchronous tools run in worker threads of the SDK; the service "
"serialises the work of a session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:46
msgid ""
"Groups are created in one call (`create_group`: elements, internal "
"connections, exposed ports), added to the service as "
"`Service.create_group`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:48
msgid ""
"**Operation** (P13.4): `execute_action`, `list_devices`, `device_status` "
"and `stop_all` are always offered; `discover_devices` and "
"`associate_devices` only when the server runs with `--enable-operation`. "
"Actions on simulated elements run directly. An action on real equipment "
"is confirmed by the user: a resolver of the SDK (`Resolve` returning "
"`Elicit`) asks the question, which works with both protocol revisions "
"(input-required results from 2026-07-28, elicitation requests before). "
"The flag `confirmed` of the service is set from the answer and never "
"appears in the input schema of the tool, so the model cannot set it. A "
"client without the elicitation capability gets a tool error and cannot "
"act on equipment. Limits and the emergency stop stay in the drivers "
"(ADR-0014); `stop_all` never asks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:57
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:59
msgid ""
"SDK 1 (`FastMCP`): superseded; its elicitation does not work with the "
"2026-07-28 revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:60
msgid ""
"One tool per element type, or a generic `call(method, args)` tool: too "
"many tools for the context of the model, or no schema to guide it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:62
msgid ""
"Requiring `context` in every call: longer requests and more mistakes from"
" the assistant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:63
msgid ""
"A blocking `run` without progress: the client times out on long runs and "
"the user sees nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:65
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:67
msgid "New operations of the service reach the assistant by adding a short tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:68
msgid ""
"The HTTP transport (P13.6) shares one server, so one session, between its"
" clients until the web instance (P14) gives each user its own session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0016-mcp-server.md:70
msgid "The SDK 2 is required: version 1 is not supported."
msgstr ""

